
 Subgraph matching, a fundamental operation in graph analytics, delivers all occurrences of a query pattern within a large data graph. Graph systems often require processing large batches of such queries simultaneously. The existing multi-query approaches typically aim to optimize this process by exploiting the maximum common subgraph (MCS) among query graphs. However, identifying MCS is computationally prohibitive and does not necessarily maximize computational reuse, leading to substantial redundancy and limited scalability. In this paper, we propose MASC, a novel framework for subgraph matching with
